(*
expect:
caught bellBounds
text bell count outside 1-8
nine also raised
finished
*)
(* tuvm#94 stage 1 — the ship's-bell convention runs 1 to 8, and a count outside
   it is a WRONG LITERAL in the node, not a load condition. So it raises rather
   than striking something the convention has no reading for.

   NOTE WHAT IS ABSENT FROM THE expect: BLOCK: no `bell: struck` line. The check
   lives in nsl (Bell>>strike:, kernel.nsl) and the prim is never reached, which
   is the whole point of putting it there — C has no bounds status code for the
   bell, unlike the display seam's 1. If this test ever prints a `bell: struck 0`,
   the check has been pushed down into C and the raise has been lost.

   The tag is asserted, not merely that something failed — an untagged catch
   would pass even if the raise came from somewhere else. Both ends of the range
   are exercised: a zero and a nine fail for the same reason but through
   different halves of the condition. *)
class BellBounds packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | bell |
    bell:: platform bell.

    [ bell strike: 0 ]
      on: [ :e | e tag = #bellBounds ]
      do: [ :e | 'caught bellBounds' out.
                 ('text ' , (e at: #text ifAbsent: [ '?' ])) out ].

    [ bell strike: 9 ]
      on: [ :e | e tag = #bellBounds ]
      do: [ :e | 'nine also raised' out ].

    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
